---- 6.1 selected specification: (1,1,1)(0,1,1)[7] ----
Selection rule, applied in this order:
   1. the specification must be ADEQUATE: its residuals must pass the
      Ljung-Box test (no predictable structure left);
   2. among adequate specifications, lowest AICc and fewest parameters;
   3. out-of-sample accuracy (rolling one-step-ahead and 4-week hold-out).
 Chosen: (1,1,1)(0,1,1)[7] with Ljung-Box p(14) = 0.371 , AICc = 11951.37 , rolling RMSE = 1270.9 and hold-out RMSE = 2008.3 .
The weekday-dummy specification forecasts slightly better one step ahead
 (rolling RMSE 1202.8 ) but its residuals are strongly autocorrelated (Ljung-Box p < 0.001),
 so it is not an adequate model and is not adopted.

